## 1.2 Session Startup Protocol

At the start of every Claude Code session, before writing any code, execute this protocol:

- Search project knowledge for 'Project Context Handoff' and read the current version summary to orient to the project state.

- Identify which Build Sequencing Plan phase is currently in progress.

- Search project knowledge for the specific specification sections relevant to the task at hand before writing any code.

- Confirm the local environment is running (make api, npm run dev) before attempting any integration test.

- Never assume a decision is unmade. Search project knowledge first.

# 2. Absolute Rules

The following rules are non-negotiable. They apply to every line of code, every API contract, and every database schema element produced for the OBS.

| **RULE 1 — Terminology is exact.**** Every identifier in code (variable names, function names, column names, enum values, API path segments, UI labels) must use the exact term from the System Context and Domain Glossary v1.11. Do not introduce synonyms. Do not abbreviate terms not already abbreviated in the glossary. Examples: use cost_center_id, not cc_id or costCenterId. Use is_finance_reviewer, not finance_reviewer_flag. Use ALL_WRITE, not write_access.** |
| --- |

| **RULE 2 — Architecture decisions are final.**** The technology stack, hosting model, authentication approach, data platform, and all decisions recorded in the Project Context Handoff v2.4 are final. Do not propose alternative frameworks, databases, or approaches. Implement what is specified. If you believe a specification contains an error or contradiction, stop and raise it as a question rather than making a unilateral change.** |
| --- |

| **RULE 3 — The frontend is a display layer only.**** No authoritative business logic lives in the frontend. No calculation result is trusted unless it came from the server-side calculation service. The frontend may show optimistic estimates while a server response is in flight. It must always reconcile to the server result. The frontend never constructs SQL, never reads the database directly, and never owns grant enforcement logic.** |
| --- |

| **RULE 4 — Business rules are stored as data, never hardcoded.**** No compensation rate, merit percentage, overhead allocation rate, or salary cap value may appear as a literal in application code. All such values are read from the obs.* configuration tables (obs.merit_increase_rates, obs.compensation_burden_rates, obs.compensation_component_mappings, obs.overhead_allocation_rates) at runtime.** |
| --- |

| **RULE 5 — Every API endpoint enforces the full 7-step authorization flow.**** Step 1: Validate Entra ID access token (or mock token in local env). HTTP 401 on failure. Step 2: Resolve user in obs.users; check is_active = TRUE. HTTP 403 on failure. Step 3: If is_administrator = TRUE, grant full access and skip Steps 4–6. Step 4: Check required capability flags for the operation class. HTTP 403 on failure. Step 5: Check cost center scope. HTTP 403 on failure. Step 6: Check standard grant (ALL_WRITE for writes) and confidential grant for compensation fields. Strip fields or HTTP 403 on failure. Step 7: Execute operation and write audit log entry. Never return HTTP 404 to obscure a resource from an unauthorized user — use HTTP 403.** |
| --- |

| **RULE 6 — Every mutation writes an audit event.**** Every create, update, and delete operation writes an append-only record to obs.audit_log. The audit log is never modified after write. No UPDATE or DELETE is ever issued against obs.audit_log. Audit events are written synchronously within the same API call as the mutation. If the audit write fails, the mutation must also fail (transaction rollback).** |
| --- |

| **RULE 7 — Notification failures are non-fatal.**** obs.notifications writes are wrapped in try/except. A notification write failure must not roll back the triggering event. Log WARNING on failure. The triggering API call returns success regardless.** |
| --- |

| **RULE 8 — The LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS safety constraint.**** LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS=true is permitted only on localhost. A startup assertion must raise an error if LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS=true and the host is not localhost. LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS cannot be set via an API call, a request header, or any runtime mechanism — it is environment variable only, read once at startup.** |
| --- |

| **RULE 9 — OBS never writes to source systems.**** No code path may write to the accounting system or HR admin system under any circumstance. obs.expense_accounts and obs.account_hierarchy_nodes have no UPDATE or DELETE API endpoints. Return HTTP 405 for any write attempt.** |
| --- |

| **RULE 10 — All ingestion operations are idempotent.**** Running the same file through the ingestion pipeline twice must produce the same result. No duplicate records. PostgreSQL INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE (atomic upsert) is the required promotion mechanism. Never use INSERT without deduplication logic. Use SHA-256 content hash + file name as the deduplication key in obs.ingestion_control.** |
| --- |

# 3. Technology Stack Quick Reference

Never deviate from this stack. All decisions are final.

| **Layer** | **Technology** | **Key Constraint** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Frontend framework** | React 18 + TypeScript | Strict TypeScript — no any types in production code. All component props must be typed. |
| **Frontend build** | Vite | vite.config.ts proxies /api/* to localhost:8000 in development. |
| **UI component library** | MUI (Material UI) v5 | Use MUI components as specified in UX spec. Do not substitute third-party component alternatives. |
| **Drag and drop** | @hello-pangea/dnd | Required for Report Column reordering in ColumnConfigurator.tsx (Reporting FR Section 5, UX Spec Section 7.6). |
| **Frontend mock API** | MSW (Mock Service Worker) | Activated by VITE_API_MOCK=true. Handlers in frontend/src/mocks/handlers.ts. |
| **Backend framework** | Python 3.11 + FastAPI | Stateless REST API. All business logic server-side. |
| **ASGI server (local)** | Uvicorn | uvicorn backend.app.main:app --reload --port 8000 |
| **Local database** | DuckDB ≥ 0.10 | Activated by DB_ENGINE=duckdb. All obs.* schemas identical to PostgreSQL production schemas. |
| **Production database** | Azure PostgreSQL Flexible Server | Activated by DB_ENGINE=postgresql. Same query logic as DuckDB path. |
| **Excel export** | openpyxl | Server-side only. Never client-side. See Reporting FR Section 11. |
| **Linter (Python)** | Ruff | Replaces Flake8 + Black. Run via make lint. |
| **Linter (TypeScript)** | ESLint + Prettier |  |
| **Type checker (Python)** | mypy | Run via make typecheck. |
| **Test runner** | pytest + pytest-asyncio | Unit tests: no running services. Integration tests: require live local API. |
| **HTTP test client** | httpx | Used in integration tests for real HTTP requests to the running local API. |

