# 5. Backend Implementation Patterns

Apply these patterns consistently across all routers and services.

## 5.1 Router Pattern

Every router follows this structure. Never put business logic in a router function — delegate to a service.

| **# backend/app/routers/budget_versions.py from fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, HTTPException from app.auth.middleware import get_current_user from app.auth.models import CurrentUser from app.db.engine import get_connection from app.models.budget import BudgetVersionResponse, CreateBudgetVersionRequest from app.services import budget_service router = APIRouter(prefix=****'****/api/v1/budget-versions****'****, tags=[****'****budget-versions****'****]) @router.get(****'****/{version_id}****'****, response_model=BudgetVersionResponse) async def get_budget_version(     version_id: str,     current_user: CurrentUser = Depends(get_current_user),     conn = Depends(get_connection), ):     # Authorization enforced inside service — passes current_user for scope checks     return budget_service.get_version(conn, version_id, current_user)** |
| --- |

## 5.2 Authorization Enforcement Pattern

Authorization is enforced as a reusable dependency and inside service functions. Never inline authorization checks in routers without a named helper.

| **# backend/app/auth/middleware.py from app.db.helpers import get_user_record from app.config import settings def get_current_user(conn=Depends(get_connection)) -****>**** CurrentUser:     if settings.LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS:         # Startup assertion elsewhere guarantees this only runs on localhost         return CurrentUser(             user_id=settings.LOCAL_AUTH_USER_ID,             email=settings.LOCAL_AUTH_USER_EMAIL,             display_name=settings.LOCAL_AUTH_USER_NAME,         )     token = _validate_entra_token()          # raises HTTP 401 on failure     user  = get_user_record(conn, token.oid) # raises HTTP 403 if not found / inactive     return user # backend/app/db/helpers.py — authorization helpers def require_administrator(user: CurrentUser):     if not user.is_administrator:         raise HTTPException(status_code=403, detail=****'****Administrator access required****'****) def require_cost_center_access(user: CurrentUser, cost_center_id: str, conn,                                 write: bool = False, confidential: bool = False):     if user.is_administrator:         return  # administrators have implicit access     # ... resolve grants, check scope, strip confidential fields ...** |
| --- |

## 5.3 Audit Write Pattern

Every mutation calls audit_write() as the final step inside the same database transaction. If audit_write() fails, the transaction rolls back.

| **# backend/app/db/helpers.py import uuid, datetime def audit_write(conn, event_type: str, user_id: str, entity_type: str,                entity_id: str, previous_value=None, new_value=None, **kwargs):     conn.execute(         ****'****INSERT INTO obs.audit_log VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)****'****,         [str(uuid.uuid4()), datetime.datetime.utcnow(), event_type, user_id,          kwargs.get(****'****session_id****'****), entity_type, entity_id,          json.dumps(previous_value), json.dumps(new_value),          kwargs.get(****'****ip_address****'****), ****'****SUCCESS****'****]     )     # obs.audit_log is append-only — never call UPDATE or DELETE on it** |
| --- |

## 5.4 Database Abstraction (DuckDB / PostgreSQL)

All queries must work identically against both DB_ENGINE=duckdb (local) and DB_ENGINE=postgresql (production). The only code that differs is inside engine.py.

| **# backend/app/db/engine.py from app.config import settings import duckdb def get_connection():     if settings.DB_ENGINE == ****'****duckdb****'****:         conn = duckdb.connect(settings.DUCKDB_PATH)         yield conn         conn.close()     elif settings.DB_ENGINE == ****'****postgresql****'****:         # production: direct PostgreSQL connection         import psycopg2, psycopg2.extras         conn = psycopg2.connect(settings.PG_CONNECTION_STRING, cursor_factory=psycopg2.extras.RealDictCursor)         ... # backend/app/db/helpers.py def merge(conn, table: str, records: list, key_cols: list):     ****'****'****'****Idempotent upsert. Uses DELETE+INSERT on DuckDB, INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE on PostgreSQL.****'****'****'****     if settings.DB_ENGINE == ****'****duckdb****'****:         _duckdb_upsert(conn, table, records, key_cols)     elif settings.DB_ENGINE == ****'****postgresql****'****:         _pg_upsert(conn, table, records, key_cols)     else:         raise RuntimeError(f****'****merge() not supported for DB_ENGINE={settings.DB_ENGINE!r}****'****)** |
| --- |

## 5.5 Calculation Service Pattern

The calculation service exposes a dry-run endpoint and a separate save endpoint. Never combine calculation and persistence in one endpoint.

| **# Pattern for every calculation: dry-run first, save separate # POST /api/v1/workforce-planning/calculate  (dry-run — no side effects) #   Body: { cost_center_id, fiscal_year, positions: [...] } #   Returns: calculated amounts for all positions, all periods #   No DB writes. No audit event. # POST /api/v1/workforce-planning/save  (persists + triggers budget line push) #   Same body as /calculate #   Saves to obs.positions #   Triggers direct push to obs.budget_lines (synchronous, same API call) #   Writes WORKFORCE_PLAN_SAVED audit event #   Requires ALL_WRITE confidential grant or Administrator # All business rule values are read from DB at calculation time: #   obs.merit_increase_rates  (rate_pct for fiscal_year) #   obs.compensation_burden_rates  (7 components + wage caps for fiscal_year) #   obs.compensation_component_mappings  (component_code → account_code)** |
| --- |

## 5.6 Notification Service Pattern

| **# backend/app/services/notification_service.py import logging logger = logging.getLogger(__name__) def create_notification(conn, user_id: str, event_type: str,                         title: str, body: str, deep_link_url: str,                         source_entity_type: str, source_entity_id: str,                         expires_at=None):     try:         conn.execute(             ****'****INSERT INTO obs.notifications VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)****'****,             [str(uuid.uuid4()), user_id, event_type, title, body,              deep_link_url, False, None, source_entity_type,              source_entity_id, expires_at]         )     except Exception as e:         logger.warning(f****'****Notification write failed (non-fatal): {e}****'****)         # Do NOT re-raise — notification failures must not roll back the triggering event def create_notifications_bulk(conn, notifications: list[dict]):     for n in notifications:         create_notification(conn, **n)  # each wrapped individually** |
| --- |

# 6. Frontend Implementation Patterns

## 6.1 Component File Conventions

Every React component follows these conventions:

- One component per file. File name matches component name (PascalCase.tsx).

- All props must have TypeScript interfaces. No implicit any.

- Use MUI components as specified in the UX Specification. Do not substitute alternatives.

- Never put API call logic directly in a component — use a custom hook or a service function from services/.

- Never store notification state in ObsUserContext — the context is for identity and capability flags only.

- BudgetWorkflowContext is session-only. It is not persisted to the server. It resets on page refresh.

## 6.2 API Client Pattern

| **// frontend/src/services/budgetService.ts const API_BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE_URL ?? ****'****'****; async function apiFetch****<****T****>****(path: string, options?: RequestInit): Promise****<****T****>**** {   const res = await fetch(****${API_BASE}${path}****, {     ...options,     headers: { ****'****Content-Type****'****: ****'****application/json****'****, ...options?.headers },   });   if (!res.ok) {     const err = await res.json().catch(() =****>**** ({ detail: res.statusText }));     throw new ApiError(res.status, err.detail ?? ****'****Unknown error****'****);   }   return res.json(); } export const budgetService = {   getVersion: (versionId: string) =****>****     apiFetch****<****BudgetVersionResponse****>****(****/api/v1/budget-versions/${versionId}****),   // ... other methods };** |
| --- |

## 6.3 Notification Bell Polling

| **// frontend/src/components/layout/NotificationBell.tsx // Poll GET /api/v1/notifications?unread_only=true****&****page_size=1 // Pause polling when document.visibilityState === ****'****hidden****'**** // Resume + immediate fetch on tab becoming visible // Store unread count in local React state — NOT in ObsUserContext // Optimistic update: mark-one-read decrements count by 1 (floor 0) //                   mark-all-read sets count to 0 // Interval configured by NOTIFICATION_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS (default 60s)** |
