## 6.4 Report Column Configurator

| **// frontend/src/components/reporting/ColumnConfigurator.tsx // Uses @hello-pangea/dnd for drag-and-drop reordering // Two arrays in state: availableColumns, reportColumns // On Add:    move item from available → report (append to end) // On Remove: move item from report → available (sorted by display_name) //            Remove button disabled when reportColumns.length === 1 // On Reorder: update reportColumns array order via drag result // On Default Visible toggle: update reportColumns[i].default_visible // On Save: serialize reportColumns → JSON → include in PATCH body as available_columns // Validation: at least one column with default_visible = TRUE //   Inline message if all toggles set to FALSE: //   ****'****At least one column must be visible by default.****'** |
| --- |

# 7. PostgreSQL / DuckDB Schema Rules

The schema/bootstrap.sql file defines all obs.* tables. Follow these rules when writing or amending schema definitions:

- All primary keys are STRING (UUID) unless the specification states otherwise.

- All timestamps are stored in UTC. Column type: TIMESTAMP.

- All monetary amounts are stored as DECIMAL(15,2).

- All percentage rates are stored as DECIMAL(6,4) (supports values like 0.0765 for 7.65%).

- All boolean columns default to FALSE unless the specification states otherwise.

- obs.audit_log is append-only. It has no UPDATE or DELETE endpoints and no application code may issue UPDATE/DELETE against it.

- obs.notifications is NOT an audit log. is_read and read_at are the only mutable columns after insert.

- obs.expense_accounts and obs.account_hierarchy_nodes are read-only via the API. HTTP 405 for any write attempt through the API layer.

## 7.1 DuckDB Upsert Substitute and PostgreSQL Upsert

PostgreSQL supports native INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE. DuckDB does not. The db/helpers.py merge() function implements DELETE + INSERT for DuckDB and INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE for PostgreSQL (_pg_upsert, the canonical implementation defined in Azure Cloud Migration Specification v2.0 Section 6.4):

| **def _duckdb_upsert(conn, table: str, records: list, key_cols: list):     if not records:         return     # Build WHERE clause from key columns     where = ****'**** AND ****'****.join(f****'****{k} = ?****'**** for k in key_cols)     for record in records:         key_values = [record[k] for k in key_cols]         conn.execute(f****'****DELETE FROM {table} WHERE {where}****'****, key_values)     # Bulk insert     cols = list(records[0].keys())     placeholders = ****'****, ****'****.join(****'****?****'**** * len(cols))     col_names = ****'****, ****'****.join(cols)     conn.executemany(         f****'****INSERT INTO {table} ({col_names}) VALUES ({placeholders})****'****,         [[r[c] for c in cols] for r in records]     )** |
| --- |

# 8. API Contract Standards

All API endpoints conform to these standards. Do not deviate.

## 8.1 URL and Method Conventions

| **Convention** | **Rule** | **Example** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Path segments** | kebab-case | /api/v1/finance-review, /api/v1/budget-versions |
| **Resource IDs** | Path parameter named {resource_id} | /api/v1/positions/{position_id} |
| **Collection reads** | GET on the collection path | GET /api/v1/positions |
| **Single resource** | GET on the resource path | GET /api/v1/positions/{position_id} |
| **Create** | POST on the collection path | POST /api/v1/positions |
| **Partial update** | PATCH on the resource path | PATCH /api/v1/positions/{position_id} |
| **Actions** | POST on action sub-path | POST /api/v1/transfers/{id}/approve |
| **All versions** | /api/v1/ prefix on all endpoints | No /api/v2/ exists in this system |

## 8.2 Error Response Format

| **# All error responses use this format: { ****'****detail****'****: ****'****Human-readable description of the error****'**** } # HTTP 401 — Token missing, expired, or invalid # HTTP 403 — Authenticated but not authorized (insufficient flags, scope, or grant) # HTTP 404 — Resource does not exist AND user would have access if it did #           NEVER return 404 to obscure a resource from an unauthorized user — use 403 # HTTP 409 — State conflict (e.g., cloning to an existing version name, deleting active version) # HTTP 422 — Validation failure (missing required fields, invalid values) # HTTP 405 — Method not allowed (e.g., write attempt on account hierarchy endpoints)** |
| --- |

## 8.3 Pagination Standard

| **# All list endpoints that may return ****>**** 50 records support pagination: # Query params: page (INT, 1-based, default 1), page_size (INT, default 50, max 200) # Response envelope: {   ****'****total_count****'****: 142,   ****'****page****'****: 1,   ****'****page_size****'****: 50,   ****'****results****'****: [ /***** array of items *****/ ] }** |
| --- |

## 8.4 Confidential Field Enforcement

Compensation fields (base_salary, burden_rate, derived compensation components, total employment cost) must be absent from response payloads — not null, absent — when the requesting user holds ALL_NONE confidential grant on the relevant cost center. This is enforced at the API response layer, not the query layer.

| **# backend/app/db/helpers.py CONFIDENTIAL_FIELDS = {     ****'****base_salary****'****, ****'****salary_adjustment****'****, ****'****aipeip_bonus****'****, ****'****other_bonus****'****,     ****'****burden_fica****'****, ****'****burden_medicare****'****, ****'****burden_suta****'****, ****'****burden_futa****'****,     ****'****burden_federal_income_tax****'****, ****'****burden_state_income_tax****'****, ****'****burden_other_benefits****'****,     ****'****total_employment_cost****'****, } def strip_confidential(record: dict, user: CurrentUser, cost_center_id: str) -****>**** dict:     if user.is_administrator:         return record     grant = get_confidential_grant(user, cost_center_id)     if grant == ****'****ALL_NONE****'****:         return {k: v for k, v in record.items() if k not in CONFIDENTIAL_FIELDS}     return record** |
| --- |

# 9. Key Calculation Rules Quick Reference

The full calculation rules are in Functional Requirements: Workforce Planning v1.1 Sections 5.1–5.3. This section provides a quick reference for the most critical rules. Always verify against the specification for full detail.

## 9.1 Salary Expense by Period

| **Period** | **Base Amount Used** | **Proration** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **January (Period 1)** | base_salary only | Prorated by days active in January |
| **February (Period 2)** | base_salary only | Prorated by days active in February |
| **March–December (3–12)** | new_annual_salary (base + merit + adjustment) | Prorated by days active in each period |

| **# new_annual_salary = base_salary + merit_increase_amount + salary_adjustment # merit_increase_amount = base_salary ***** (merit_rate_pct / 100) # merit_rate_pct comes from obs.merit_increase_rates for the fiscal_year # proration_factor_m = days_active_in_month_m / days_in_month_m # days_active = MIN(last_day_of_month, end_date or last_day_of_year) #             - MAX(first_day_of_month, start_date) + 1 # If days_active ******<******= 0, proration_factor = 0 # monthly_salary_m = (annual_salary_for_period / 12) ***** proration_factor_m # Round to 2 decimal places** |
| --- |

## 9.2 AIPEIP Bonus Proration Rules

- Active positions: AIPEIP bonus is not prorated by month. Full annual amount across all active periods.

- Termination: AIPEIP bonus is zeroed for the entire fiscal year (all 12 periods).

- Retirement: AIPEIP bonus is prorated through the retirement month. Months after the retirement effective_date are zero.

- Proration for retirement: monthly_aipeip_m = (aipeip_bonus / 12) for months 1 through retirement month; 0 thereafter.

## 9.3 Burden Rate Calculation

| **# For each burden component c: #   If component has a wage cap (FICA, SUTA, FUTA): #     burdened_salary_c = MIN(new_annual_salary, wage_cap_c) #   Else (Medicare, state income tax, federal income tax, other benefits): #     burdened_salary_c = new_annual_salary # annual_burden_c = burdened_salary_c ***** (rate_pct_c / 100) ***** fte # monthly_burden_c_m = (annual_burden_c / 12) * proration_factor_m # Round each component monthly amount to 2 decimal places # Each component maps to a separate budget line via obs.compensation_component_mappings # component_code examples: ****'****burden_fica****'****, ****'****burden_medicare****'****, ****'****burden_suta****'****, etc.** |
| --- |

## 9.4 Direct Push to Budget Lines

Every position save triggers a synchronous direct push. This is not a background job.

| **# After saving to obs.positions: # For each position in the cost center (for the fiscal_year): #   For each planning period m (1..12): #     For each compensation component c: #       Compute amount per Section 5 rules #       Write/update obs.budget_lines with: #         is_calculated = TRUE #         source = ****'****workforce_planning****'**** #         account_code = obs.compensation_component_mappings[c].account_code # Use merge() — not INSERT — to handle updates to existing lines # If a component mapping is missing, skip and log WARNING (do not fail the save)** |
| --- |

# 10. Ingestion Pipeline Rules

The full pipeline specification is in Data Integration Specification v1.6. These are the critical rules Claude Code must not get wrong.

| **Rule** | **Behaviour** | **Specification Reference** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **File deduplication** | SHA-256 of raw file bytes + file_name. Same content = process once. Computed before any parsing. | DI Spec v1.5 Section 7.2 |
| **Sheet selection — Excel** | Actuals: sheet named 'Budget-Accounting'. Employees: sheet named 'Budget-HR'. Reject if named sheet absent. | DI Spec v1.5 Section 2.3 |
| **Non-USD currency** | Actuals records with currency != 'USD' are rejected and quarantined as malformed. Not warned, not promoted. | DI Spec v1.5 Section 3.2 (OI-DI-03) |
| **Error rate threshold** | If invalid rows > 80% of total rows: reject entire file. If <= 80%: promote valid rows, quarantine invalid. | DI Spec v1.5 Section 7.3.3 |
| **Quarantine re-promotion** | Automatic — when an Administrator adds a missing dimension, the pipeline detects the resolution and re-promotes without manual trigger. | DI Spec v1.5 Section 7.4 (OI-DI-05) |
| **Alert channels** | Pipeline alert events notify both Microsoft Teams (incoming webhook) AND Email. Both required. Console-only in local env. | DI Spec v1.5 Section 9 (OI-DI-04) |
| **Post-seed hierarchy** | After initial cost center hierarchy seed, re-import of hierarchy files is not supported. API returns HTTP 405. | DI Spec v1.5 (OI-DI-06) |
| **Import sequencing** | Account hierarchy and actuals operate on independent schedules. Quarantine handles sequencing gaps. | DI Spec v1.5 Section 6.6 (OI-DI-07) |

# 11. Testing Requirements

Testing requirements are fully specified in the Local Development Environment Specification v1.1 Section 10. This section provides the key constraints Claude Code must observe.

## 11.1 AC Registry

Every AC-* identifier from every specification must have an entry in backend/tests/ac_registry.yaml. The make ac-coverage command must exit 0 before any phase is considered complete.

| **# backend/tests/ac_registry.yaml — required format AC-CAP-01:   file: integration/test_auth.py   test: test_administrator_has_full_access   phase: 1 AC-DI-55:   file: integration/test_pipeline.py   test: test_non_usd_records_rejected_and_quarantined   phase: 2** |
| --- |

## 11.2 Calculation Service — 100% Unit Test Coverage

The calculation service has a 100% line coverage requirement. Every compensation calculation rule, proration formula, merit rate application, burden rate formula, wage cap, and AIPEIP proration case must have a dedicated unit test. Use pytest parametrize to cover boundary conditions (e.g., position starting on the first day of a month, last day of a month, spanning the March merit effective date).

## 11.3 Integration Test Database Isolation

Integration tests use local-data/obs-test.duckdb — never local-data/obs.duckdb. The test database is bootstrapped and seeded fresh at the start of each test session via a session-scoped pytest fixture. Individual tests use transaction rollback or targeted cleanup to restore state between tests.

# 12. Compensation Burden Components Reference

These are the exact component_code values used in obs.compensation_component_mappings and in obs.budget_lines. Use them exactly — do not abbreviate or rename.

| **component_code** | **Wage Cap Applies?** | **Rate Source Column in obs.compensation_burden_rates** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **salary** | N/A — not a burden component | N/A — mapped via obs.compensation_component_mappings |
| **aipeip_bonus** | N/A | N/A |
| **other_bonus** | N/A | N/A |
| **burden_fica** | Yes — fica_wage_cap | fica_rate_pct |
| **burden_medicare** | No | medicare_rate_pct |
| **burden_suta** | Yes — suta_wage_cap | suta_rate_pct |
| **burden_futa** | Yes — futa_wage_cap | futa_rate_pct |
| **burden_state_income_tax** | No | state_income_tax_rate_pct |
| **burden_federal_income_tax** | No | federal_income_tax_rate_pct |
| **burden_other_benefits** | No | other_benefits_rate_pct |

# 13. Finance Approval Workflow — resolve_budget_version_status()

This server-side helper is called after every approve or reject action. It must be implemented as a discrete function — not inlined in the approve/reject route handlers.

| **def resolve_budget_version_status(conn, version_id: str):     ****'****'****'****     Called after every approve or reject action.     Evaluates all obs.finance_review_records for the version.     Transitions obs.budget_versions.status if all records have resolved.     ****'****'****'****     records = conn.execute(         ****'****SELECT status FROM obs.finance_review_records WHERE version_id = ?****'****,         [version_id]     ).fetchall()     statuses = {r[0] for r in records}     if ****'****pending****'**** in statuses:         return  # still waiting — no version status change     if ****'****rejected****'**** in statuses:         # At least one rejection and no pending — version is rejected         _set_version_status(conn, version_id, ****'****Rejected****'****)         audit_write(conn, ****'****BUDGET_VERSION_REJECTED****'****, ****'****system****'****, ****'****BudgetVersion****'****, version_id)     else:         # All approved         _set_version_status(conn, version_id, ****'****Approved****'****)         audit_write(conn, ****'****BUDGET_VERSION_APPROVED****'****, ****'****system****'****, ****'****BudgetVersion****'****, version_id)** |
| --- |

# 14. Phase Gate Checklist

Before declaring any phase complete, verify all items on this checklist. No phase may be marked complete with any unchecked item.

## 14.1 Per-Phase Gate

- All deliverables listed in Build Sequencing Plan v1.1 for the phase are implemented.

- All API endpoints listed in the phase are implemented and return correct responses.

- All PostgreSQL tables listed in the phase exist with correct schemas (run make db-bootstrap and verify).

- make test-unit passes with 0 failures. Calculation service has 100% line coverage (Phase 4 onwards).

- make test-integration passes with 0 failures.

- make ac-coverage exits 0 (all AC-* identifiers for this phase are registered and passing).

- make lint passes with 0 errors (Python ruff + TypeScript ESLint).

- make typecheck passes with 0 errors (mypy + tsc --noEmit).

- No hardcoded rate values, no LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS in non-local code paths.

- Every mutation in this phase writes the correct audit event — verified by integration test querying obs.audit_log.

## 14.2 Additional Gates — Specific Phases

| **Phase** | **Additional Gate** | **Verification Method** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Phase 0** | All 29 obs.* tables exist and are queryable | make db-bootstrap; SELECT count(*) from each table |
| **Phase 1** | Last-active-Administrator guard enforced | Integration test: attempt to deactivate the only admin — expect HTTP 409 |
| **Phase 2** | Ingestion pipeline idempotency verified | Run same fixture file twice; row count unchanged |
| **Phase 4** | Personnel expense direct push is synchronous | Integration test: save position; immediately query obs.budget_lines |
| **Phase 4** | Transfer expiry background logic sets correct status | Unit test with mocked clock advancing 3+ days |
| **Phase 5** | Permanent version delete is transactional | Integration test: verify budget_lines, targets, vendor_line_items all removed |
| **Phase 6** | resolve_budget_version_status() tested for all state combinations | Unit tests: all approved; mixed approved+rejected; some pending |
| **Phase 7** | Notification failures do not roll back triggering event | Integration test: simulate notification write error; triggering event succeeds |
| **Phase 8** | Excel export confidential field exclusion | Integration test: export as user with ALL_NONE grant; verify absent columns |
| **Phase 10** | API deploys to Azure App Service and starts cleanly under production configuration | Deploy to App Service; run make test-integration against the deployed target |

# 15. Common Pitfalls — Do Not Do These

| **Do not use HTTP 404 to hide unauthorized resources.**** Always return HTTP 403 when a resource exists but the user is not authorized. HTTP 404 is only for genuinely non-existent resources that the user would have access to if they existed.** |
| --- |

| **Do not hardcode any rate, cap, or mapping value.**** Every numeric business rule comes from the database. obs.merit_increase_rates, obs.compensation_burden_rates, obs.compensation_component_mappings, obs.overhead_allocation_rates. No literals.** |
| --- |

| **Do not combine the dry-run calculation and the save in one endpoint.**** The calculation service must expose POST /calculate (no side effects) and POST /save (persists + audits) as separate endpoints. The frontend calls /calculate on field changes and /save only on explicit user action.** |
| --- |

| **Do not write UPDATE or DELETE against obs.audit_log.**** The audit log is append-only. No application code path may issue UPDATE or DELETE on obs.audit_log under any circumstance. If you find yourself needing to do this, you have made a design error.** |
| --- |

| **Do not put notification state in ObsUserContext.**** ObsUserContext holds identity and capability flags only. Notification state (unread_count, inbox items) lives in local React state within NotificationBell.tsx.** |
| --- |

| **Do not allow LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS outside localhost.**** The startup check must run at application boot, not at request time. If settings.LOCAL_AUTH_BYPASS is True and the application is not on localhost, raise an exception and refuse to start.** |
| --- |

| **Do not accept user_id as a query parameter in GET /api/v1/notifications.**** The notification API always injects WHERE user_id = :authenticated_user_id server-side. A user parameter in the query string would allow cross-user notification access and is a security vulnerability.** |
| --- |

| **Do not use WidthType.PERCENTAGE in any docx generation (openpyxl export).**** Excel column widths must use explicit numeric values. Percentage-based widths are incompatible with some consumers. This applies to the openpyxl Excel export service.** |
| --- |

